# Tappa — docker build context.
#
# 🔴 THIS FILE EXCLUDES ONLY PATHS GIT ALREADY IGNORES, AND THAT RESTRAINT IS THE
# WHOLE POINT. The build identity M8-01 shipped comes from Go's own -buildvcs, which
# reads .git INSIDE the builder; and `go build` decides vcs.modified from
# `git status --porcelain`. Excluding a TRACKED path here would make git see it as
# DELETED in the build context, so every image — including one built by CI from a
# clean checkout of a tagged commit — would stamp vcs.modified=true and log the
# "compiled from a MODIFIED working tree" WARN that cmd/tappa/main.go reserves for
# untraceable builds. Measured both ways; see the control build in this task's report.
#
# For the same reason .git itself is NOT excluded. Without it the toolchain omits
# vcs.revision entirely (no error, no warning) and the shipped artifact stops being
# traceable to a commit at all — silently undoing the one thing M8-01 added that
# nothing else in the product can reconstruct.

# --- build artifacts (gitignored) ---
bin/
dist/
*.exe
*.test
coverage.*

# --- local tooling downloaded by `make tools` (gitignored) ---
# The builder fetches its own linux/amd64 Tailwind binary; a macOS one copied in
# would be the wrong architecture and `make css` would fail confusingly.
.tools/

# --- generated CSS (gitignored; `make css` regenerates it in the builder) ---
web/static/css/app.css

# --- secrets: NEVER in an image layer (CLAUDE.md §4.7) ---
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
*.aes

# --- local editor/agent overrides (gitignored) ---
.claude/settings.local.json
.DS_Store
